From 42064b3950ec3fd622227f557d26bc7e0ca71361 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harsha Nanda <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 13:05:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(push): budget pre-push tests above measured suite runtime

`forge push` capped the package-level `test` script at a hardcoded
120000 ms. The full local suite legitimately takes ~10 minutes on
Windows, so the cap killed a healthy run mid-suite: spawnSync returned
`status: null`, `status === 0` evaluated false, and the push aborted with
no summary and no push at all.

The run is now budgeted from `resolveFullSuiteTimeoutMs()` in
scripts/test.js, and that shared default is raised from 10 to 25 minutes.
The old default sat BELOW the measured healthy runtime (602.43s for 8038
tests, Windows, pinned Bun 1.3.12, 2026-08-26), so it SIGKILLed passing
suites in both consumers. The ceiling exists to catch an indefinite hang
(issue 8aef79e8), not to bound normal runtime, so it now carries >2x
headroom over the recorded measurement; FORGE_TEST_TIMEOUT_MS still
overrides. Regressions assert the effective budget clears the measured
runtime, so a future shave fails a test instead of a user's push.

A test run terminated by a timeout, signal, or spawn error now reports
what happened rather than failing silently.

Issue: e26dbb91-0443-4e53-946e-a9941ec30ca3

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
